new file mode 100644
index 00000000..7d7338cd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/kdesu/AUTHENTICATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,111 @@
+# Android-authorized command execution
+
+The production dialog launches the optional protected native helper
+`/usr/libexec/navi-auth/authorize` with no arguments and private stdin/stdout pipes.
+It needs no listening socket or boot daemon. The helper owns phone verification
+and command execution; KDE selects the phone or password path and never turns a
+phone response into a successful su password check.
+
+The Android session owns the native setuid launcher, `rootauth.py`, protected
+trust, revocation and deployment. This GUI package does not install that authority
+or modify sudo, pkexec or PAM. Safe previews cannot launch it; their historical
+notification-only interface is described in [NOTIFICATIONS.md](NOTIFICATIONS.md).
+
+## Eligibility and wire format
+
+The first implementation accepts visible commands that round-trip the original
+bytes through UTF-8, target root, use normal scheduling/priority 50, and do not
+request terminal output. Unsupported requests retain the existing password path.
+
+The client requires the fixed path to be a root-owned regular executable with the
+setuid bit, no group/world write permissions, and a safe root-owned directory chain
+through `/`. Symlinks are rejected. There is no runtime path/UID override. The native
+launcher independently requires an original nonroot real UID and effective root,
+derives the caller from `getuid()`, sanitizes environment/groups/FDs/cwd and invokes
+the fixed protected Python backend in isolated mode.
+
+One process carries one UUID and UTF-8 JSON lines using `navi-auth-exec/v1`.
+KDE starts it from `/` with only fixed PATH/LANG; the requested execution cwd and
+GUI environment travel inside the signed operation, not inherited authority.
+Starts are limited to64KiB and reply lines to16KiB. Stdout is protocol-only;
+stderr stays separate and is drained without being interpreted as authentication.
+
+```json
+{
+  "protocol": "navi-auth-exec/v1",
+  "event": "start",
+  "request_id": "085e5872-32ad-4e08-baf7-17f86e88576d",
+  "context": {
+    "application": "Codex",
+    "action_id": "org.kde.kdesu.run",
+    "command": "printf approved",
+    "command_hidden": false,
+    "requesting_user": "alice",
+    "requesting_uid": 1000,
+    "target_user": "root",
+    "source": "kdesu",
+    "requester_pid": 123,
+    "requester_executable": "/path/to/codex",
+    "icon_name": "codex",
+    "icon_png_base64": "<optional bounded PNG>"
+  },
+  "cwd": "/home/alice",
+  "environment": {}
+}
+```
+
+`cwd` and `environment` are always present. KDE forwards actual values, when set,
+for DISPLAY, WAYLAND_DISPLAY, DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, and
+XAUTHORITY. The broker validates those values, holds the working directory, signs
+the operation, and uses a minimal execution environment. It derives the invoking
+user from the native launcher's kernel-derived real UID. Requester/application metadata remains display context,
+not proof of application identity. The same requester icon is used in the KDE
+header and signed phone context; target icon overrides do not affect it.
+
+## One execution owner
+
+Every reply must match the protocol and request ID. The broker sends `ready` only
+after verifying the phone signature, but it cannot execute until KDE sends
+`commit`. KDE atomically disables password/Run-as-me before sending that commit.
+
+Password or Run-as-me selected first sends `cancel`, waits for `canceled` or a
+precommit helper exit, and only then invokes the existing alternative. A late ready
+in that state is ignored. Closing the dialog before commit withdraws the request.
+
+After commit, the phone branch is exclusive. `executed` with a positive integer
+`pid` acknowledges that the broker launched the child. KDE returns success through
+a distinct `PhoneExecuted` result, before password caching or any call to
+`system()`, kdesud, or `SuProcess::exec()`. This is a launch acknowledgement, not the
+eventual command exit status. Acknowledgement loss cannot trigger another execution.
+
+An `error` before commit restores password fallback. An error, invalid response,
+timeout or disconnect after commit means the result is uncertain: the dialog
+offers Close, with both execution alternatives disabled. The client never replays
+the operation. Startup is bounded to1.5s; the precommit wait is125s while the helper
+enforces strict120s approval/commit expiry. Sending commit starts a separate20s
+completion deadline for signed receipt delivery and final executed, which does not
+extend approval freshness.
+
+Closing the write pipe withdraws an uncommitted request. Cancellation/terminal
+output must be flushed before helper exit. KDE allows35s precommit cleanup grace
+before best-effort termination signals and never equates signal attempts with ACK.
+A running QProcess is reaped asynchronously, never destroyed in a way that blocks
+the GUI; a normalized-root helper may reject GUI signals. No force-kill occurs
+after commit. The native helper has its own absolute180s alarm. Approved commands
+have detached sessions and stdio so helper/dialog exit cannot kill them or keep
+protocol pipes open. The client drains final buffered stdout before handling exit;
+exit0 without matching executed is never a launch acknowledgement.
+
+## Validation
+
+The existing dialog tests still run. `kdesu_phoneauth_test` uses an unprivileged
+stdio child fixture through a test-only subclass. The fixture is never installed;
+no real protected helper, phone, password check or privileged command is used.
+Coverage includes helper-path rejection, exact context/cwd/environment,
+ready/commit ordering, distinct phone completion, cancellation races, invalid
+replies, final-output draining and exclusive postcommit failure.
+
+```sh
+cmake --build ../build/kde-cli-tools --target kdesu_executable kdesu_dialog_test kdesu_phoneauth_test kdesu_dialog_preview -j8
+ctest --test-dir ../build/kde-cli-tools -R '^kdesu_(dialog|phoneauth)_test$' --output-on-failure
+```
